  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c300.html",
  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 302.30 Propane",
  "priorExpiration": "2015-06-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 302.30 “Propane” means a 3-carbon alkane gas (C3H8), that when stored under pressure inside a tank, is a colorless, odorless liquid. It is obtained as a by-product from the refining of petroleum or from natural gas processing. Propane is the main component of liquefied petroleum gas.\n\nSource. #10753, INTERIM, eff 1-1-15, EXPIRED: 6-30-15\n\nNew. #10890, eff 7-16-15 ss by #13186, eff 4-7-21 (formerly Saf-C 302.27); ss by #13186, eff 4-7-21 (formerly Saf-C 302.27)",
